UBSA(4)                  BSD Kernel Interfaces Manual                  UBSA(4)

NNAAMMEE
     uubbssaa — USB support for Belkin serial adapters

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee uuccoomm
           ddeevviiccee uubbssaa

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           ubsa_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uubbssaa driver provides support for the USB-to-RS232 Bridge chip used by
     a variety of serial adapters from Belkin and other vendors.

     The device is accessed through the ucom(4) driver which makes it behave
     like a tty(4).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The uubbssaa driver supports the following adapters:

     ••   AnyData ADU-500A EV-DO modem
     ••   AnyData ADU-E100A (no EV-DO mode support)
     ••   Belkin F5U103
     ••   Belkin F5U120
     ••   e-Tek Labs Kwik232
     ••   GoHubs GoCOM232
     ••   Peracom single port serial adapter

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/ttyU*       for callin ports
     /dev/ttyU*.init
     /dev/ttyU*.lock  corresponding callin initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

     /dev/cuaU*       for callout ports
     /dev/cuaU*.init
     /dev/cuaU*.lock  corresponding callout initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     tty(4), ucom(4), usb(4)

